          "reason": "The locally checked Proofs.lean theorem slice_of_update composes original new, write_slice, and checksum. It explicitly assumes the entire arbitrary-input write_slice contract. Finish that single prerequisite, then instantiate the implication to prove the full root contract.",
          "statement": null,
          "target": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
          "theorem": null
        },
        {
          "goal": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
          "id": "chunks_partition",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "needs": [],
          "reason": "The actual pinned chunks_exact model recursively uses List.toChunksExact. The caller needs exact full-chunk lengths, byte conservation, and a remainder smaller than the chunk size.",
          "statement": "∀ {α : Type} (n : Nat) (hn : 0 < n) (xs : List α), (List.toChunksExact n hn xs).1.flatten ++ (List.toChunksExact n hn xs).2 = xs ∧ (∀ c ∈ (List.toChunksExact n hn xs).1, c.length = n) ∧ (List.toChunksExact n hn xs).2.length < n",
          "target": null,
          "theorem": "AdlerProof.chunks_partition"
        },
        {
          "goal": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
          "id": "chunks_exact",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "needs": [
            "chunks_partition"
          ],
          "reason": "The original write_slice/compute attempt stopped at core.slice.Slice.chunks_exact. This checked WP rule advances that actual call and supplies its loop and remainder bounds.",
          "statement": "∀ {α : Type} (s : Slice α) (n : Usize), 0 < n.val → core.slice.Slice.chunks_exact s n ⦃ fun it => (it.chunks.map Slice.val).flatten ++ it.remainder.val = s.val ∧ (∀ c ∈ it.chunks, c.val.length = n.val) ∧ it.remainder.val.length < n.val ⦄",
          "target": null,
          "theorem": "AdlerProof.chunks_exact_spec"
        },
        {
          "goal": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
          "id": "lane_from",
          "kind": "contract",
